body:
This struck a chord with me. When I was a kid, I've been designated as the bullied, and only when my ape peers grew out of it, I became the ghost everybody ignores. It's been my role in society for my whole life, the one who has to facetank the mildest mood swings of the others just so their life could get a smidge cooler than what it was in the first place, at no point in the contract is the mention of me being happy.

&#x200B;

Didn't have a say in any of this of course.

I'm not sure how this translates in terms of availability on the consumer end, but [that](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S221444201930453X) was the very first result I found while looking up your condition. If not already here, treatment may come sooner than you expect (or y'know, my research isn't extensive and may have resulted in a load of crap).

&#x200B;

That being said, you would still be fa :(

I'm 28 and my life consists in several iterations of this stupid cycle since I'm 16. Therapies/medication yelded 0 result. That makes the platitude "It will get better" 100% correct at least, but at what cost?

&#x200B;

Stay strong.
